      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὑμεῖς δὲ οἱ πάσχοντες ἕνεκεν τοῦ ὀνόματος δοξ⸢άζειν⸣ ὀφείλετε τὸν Θεόν",
          "english_quote": "You who suffer for the name should glorify God.",
          "issue": "“Should” can present glorifying God as advice rather than the obligation expressly stated by ὀφείλετε. The simplified edition should retain that obligatory force independently of the standard edition.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “You who suffer for the name must glorify God.” Review this proposed wording against the clause before adoption.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἐκ δὲ τοῦ ὄρους τοῦ ἑνδεκάτου",
          "english_quote": "Greek/mixed continuous text, with bounded Amherst evidence only where it actually overlaps.",
          "issue": "The unit-level theological rationale blurs this section's exclusively Greek source basis with the Greek/Latin basis of later sections. The supplied report identifies S.9.xxviii as Greek, and the reported Amherst overlap does not cover this section.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use a unit-specific statement identifying the printed Greek working source and its editorial marks; explicitly state that the supplied Amherst comparison does not overlap this section.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἐκ δὲ τοῦ ὄρους τοῦ ἑνδεκάτου, οὗ ἦσαν δένδρα καρπῶν πλήρη, ἄλλοις καὶ ἄλλοις καρποῖς κεκοσμημένα, οἱ πιστεύσαντες τοιοῦτοί εἰσιν·",
          "english_quote": "Retain name-bearing suffering, healing and gift language, infant innocence, stone/root/wealth imagery and all critical footnotes without turning editorial supply into unanimous manuscript text.",
          "issue": "The simplification metadata claims retention of infant innocence and stone/root/wealth imagery, none of which occurs in the selected section or its supplied English translation. This imports descriptions of other units into this unit's fidelity record.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the unrelated imagery from this unit's metadata. Describe only the retained fruit imagery, suffering for the name, denial/confession contrast, healing of sins, gift of life, and editorial disclosures actually present here.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions cover the selected Greek clauses and preserve the principal assertions, negations, speakers, and reader-facing servant terminology. The fruit-reading and restored-blessing notes accurately reflect the supplied project reports; their disclosed working readings need not be replaced merely because alternatives exist. Revision is needed for inaccurate unit-level metadata and, in the simplified edition, clearer obligation language. This review evaluates the supplied text and attributed reports, not unseen manuscripts or exhaustive collation. Proposed corrections remain subject to fresh review."
